1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:04,000
NEAR Intents settled $1.30B in the last 30 days.

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:07,800
Does any of it reach the NEAR token?

3
00:00:08,200 --> 00:00:13,200
We read the chain: every swap, straight from intents.near's event logs.

4
00:00:13,200 --> 00:00:17,800
Every chart is one click from the query behind it.

5
00:00:18,200 --> 00:00:24,000
Captured revenue is $26.2M a year: 0.43% of NEAR's market cap.

6
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:29,600
Now stress-test it: drag the volume up.

7
00:00:29,600 --> 00:00:35,800
It takes 4.7× today's volume to reach 2% of market cap. Real infrastructure, thin value.

8
00:00:36,200 --> 00:00:41,800
About 35% of reported volume isn't in public events.

9
00:00:41,800 --> 00:00:47,400
The obvious story: Confidential Intents. But it sits near zero until 2026-09-01.

10
00:00:47,400 --> 00:00:52,900
That day: 0.1% before, 21% after. Public volume moved -10%.

11
00:00:52,900 --> 00:00:57,800
Users moving, or a data change? We can't tell, so we say so.

12
00:00:58,200 --> 00:01:04,000
We also say what would change our mind: four triggers, with today's readings.

13
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:09,800
Today, none of the four have triggered.

14
00:01:10,200 --> 00:01:14,400
One command re-runs it all: no accounts, no keys.

15
00:01:14,400 --> 00:01:19,400
It rebuilds every metric from the committed snapshots, then rewrites the thesis.

16
00:01:19,400 --> 00:01:24,000
Same inputs, same output: the thesis comes out identical. (Sped up 2.2x.)

17
00:01:26,500 --> 00:01:33,500
Ask the chain. Show the work. What would change your mind?
